{
  "source": "course-assets/creative-thinking/creative-thinking.mp4",
  "duration": 188.1386875,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 3.24,
      "text": "Think back to the last time someone told you, good idea."
    },
    {
      "start": 3.98,
      "end": 6.88,
      "text": "It feels great to hear, but why did they actually say it?"
    },
    {
      "start": 7.82,
      "end": 12.02,
      "text": "Most likely you saw something they missed, or you found a more effective way to move forward."
    },
    {
      "start": 12.66,
      "end": 19.2,
      "text": "It's the ability to see a problem differently, question the obvious approach, and find an angle other people missed."
    },
    {
      "start": 20.14,
      "end": 24.96,
      "text": "We often assume this kind of thinking belongs strictly to artists, writers, and musicians."
    },
    {
      "start": 25.58,
      "end": 28.26,
      "text": "But problem solving requires the exact same skill."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.26,
      "end": 34.6,
      "text": "Take Steve Jobs. He wasn't a painter or a novelist. But he was highly effective at finding new angles."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.2,
      "end": 40.16,
      "text": "He looked at early, complicated desktop computers and saw a possibility others overlooked."
    },
    {
      "start": 40.74,
      "end": 43.88,
      "text": "They could be simplified, made personal, and easy to use."
    },
    {
      "start": 44.74,
      "end": 51.08,
      "text": "True creativity is noticing the gaps and possibilities that everyone else walks right past, regardless of your profession."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.0,
      "end": 55.42,
      "text": "Creativity isn't a job title or an innate personality trait."
    },
    {
      "start": 55.98,
      "end": 60.54,
      "text": "It is a habit of thinking that kicks in whenever a standard answer simply isn't enough."
    },
    {
      "start": 61.44,
      "end": 65.02,
      "text": "This graphic breaks down how that habit looks across four distinct fields."
    },
    {
      "start": 65.78,
      "end": 66.54,
      "text": "Look at the top left."
    },
    {
      "start": 67.26,
      "end": 71.72,
      "text": "A lawyer examines the exact same case file, laws, and facts as everyone else,"
    },
    {
      "start": 71.72,
      "end": 73.78,
      "text": "but finds a completely new strategy."
    },
    {
      "start": 74.7,
      "end": 77.2,
      "text": "Next to that, an entrepreneur surveys the market,"
    },
    {
      "start": 77.48,
      "end": 79.8,
      "text": "spots a consumer need that everyone else overlooked,"
    },
    {
      "start": 79.8,
      "end": 82.08,
      "text": "and builds a new way to meet it."
    },
    {
      "start": 82.54,
      "end": 83.48,
      "text": "Down on the bottom left,"
    },
    {
      "start": 83.78,
      "end": 85.7,
      "text": "when standard blueprints hit a dead end,"
    },
    {
      "start": 85.98,
      "end": 87.44,
      "text": "an engineer designs a solution"
    },
    {
      "start": 87.44,
      "end": 88.98,
      "text": "that sidesteps the roadblock."
    },
    {
      "start": 89.72,
      "end": 92.18,
      "text": "And finally, a doctor can look at a common set"
    },
    {
      "start": 92.18,
      "end": 93.96,
      "text": "of symptoms and deduce a diagnosis"
    },
    {
      "start": 93.96,
      "end": 95.7,
      "text": "that others completely missed."
    },
    {
      "start": 96.58,
      "end": 97.66,
      "text": "Across all these fields,"
    },
    {
      "start": 97.88,
      "end": 99.68,
      "text": "the difference between an average result"
    },
    {
      "start": 99.68,
      "end": 101.86,
      "text": "and an exceptional one comes down"
    },
    {
      "start": 101.86,
      "end": 103.0,
      "text": "to this habit of thinking."
    },
    {
      "start": 103.82,
      "end": 105.64,
      "text": "Today, we have artificial intelligence."
    },
    {
      "start": 105.98,
      "end": 107.08,
      "text": "You can type a prompt"
    },
    {
      "start": 107.08,
      "end": 109.54,
      "text": "and get a polished standard answer in seconds."
    },
    {
      "start": 110.08,
      "end": 111.8,
      "text": "But getting an answer is only the beginning."
    },
    {
      "start": 112.6,
      "end": 114.58,
      "text": "Your advantage is noticing what's missing,"
    },
    {
      "start": 114.94,
      "end": 116.48,
      "text": "connecting ideas from different places,"
    },
    {
      "start": 116.72,
      "end": 118.12,
      "text": "and choosing a better direction."
    },
    {
      "start": 118.76,
      "end": 120.82,
      "text": "That human advantage isn't a magic gift."
    },
    {
      "start": 121.2,
      "end": 123.16,
      "text": "You can actively build and improve it"
    },
    {
      "start": 123.16,
      "end": 125.06,
      "text": "through specific daily practice."
    },
    {
      "start": 125.78,
      "end": 127.88,
      "text": "This guide outlines four concrete habits"
    },
    {
      "start": 127.88,
      "end": 129.94,
      "text": "you can use to generate better solutions."
    },
    {
      "start": 130.62,
      "end": 132.4,
      "text": "The first habit, shown on the top left,"
    },
    {
      "start": 132.82,
      "end": 134.76,
      "text": "is to generate before you judge."
    },
    {
      "start": 135.32,
      "end": 136.54,
      "text": "Write down several ideas,"
    },
    {
      "start": 136.54,
      "end": 142.04,
      "text": "including the bad ones, before you decide what works. The most obvious, standard ideas usually"
    },
    {
      "start": 142.04,
      "end": 149.22,
      "text": "arrive first. Next, on the top right, ask what if. Take one core rule or assumption about your"
    },
    {
      "start": 149.22,
      "end": 154.62,
      "text": "problem and change it. See what happens if the exact opposite were true. Third, on the bottom"
    },
    {
      "start": 154.62,
      "end": 160.28,
      "text": "left, connect unrelated things. Look for a pattern, feature, or approach from a completely"
    },
    {
      "start": 160.28,
      "end": 165.84,
      "text": "different industry and try applying it to your current roadblock. Finally, step away, then"
    },
    {
      "start": 165.84,
      "end": 171.08,
      "text": "return. Focus intensely on the problem and then go take a walk or switch tasks."
    },
    {
      "start": 171.64,
      "end": 175.14,
      "text": "New mental connections often form in the background when your attention moves"
    },
    {
      "start": 175.14,
      "end": 179.52,
      "text": "elsewhere. These four habits widen your options. Then judgment picks the"
    },
    {
      "start": 179.52,
      "end": 183.66,
      "text": "one that fits. AI widens the options. You still pick the better angle."
    }
  ],
